# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc atan. The rule atan(tan(a)) = a-n*pi took n = floor(a/pi+1/2) from the double of a (usual.cc:764-766 of the stock tarball), which has 16 digits: atan(tan(10^15)) gave 10^15-318309886183790*pi, 2.10969811707, outside (-pi/2, pi/2) (right -1.03189453652, n one higher); 10^17 gave -216.29, 30! a number near 2.8e17; next to the pole a/pi+1/2 = 1-10^-15/pi rounded to 1 in the double, so atan(tan(pi/2-10^-15)) gave pi/2-10^-15-pi, -1.5708 (right +1.5708), and degree mode the same with 180. Now a/pi+1/2 (re(a) for a complex a) is evaluated at Digits plus its own digits plus 20, 40, ... 1280, and n is taken when two levels in a row give the same floor, each clear of an integer by more than 10^10 units of its last digit; otherwise atan stays unevaluated and evalf gives the principal value. atan(tan(2)) = 2-pi and atan(tan(x)) for a free x keep their form.
# Changed by Pascaline contributors, 2026-11-05
